[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
id = &"economy"
title = "Resources and gathering"
order = 80
summary = "Four resources, and why the walk back is the part that costs you."
body = "Four resources: FOOD, WOOD, GOLD and STONE. What each thing costs is on the
Troops and Buildings pages.

Gathering is a ROUND TRIP. A crew walks to a node, works it, fills up, walks
back to a drop-off and unloads. So distance is income: a node across the map
earns a fraction of what the same node beside your town does, and the
difference is the walk, every trip, all match.

A storehouse is a drop-off you can put anywhere. It is usually far cheaper
than moving your economy to the resources.

## Nodes run out

Trees hold little and go quickly; gold and stone last a long time. When a
crew works a tree out it retargets itself to the nearest surviving node of
the SAME kind close by — it will never switch you from wood to food behind
your back. When nothing of that kind is left in reach it stops, and a stopped
crew is waiting for orders.

## The ground says what grows on it

Forests sit where it is wet, orchards through the middle, dry trees and palms
on sand, and stone at the foot of mountains. Which means you can read where
somebody's resources must be from terrain you have only glimpsed.

## Casualties cut income

A crew gathers per LIVING soldier. Raiding gatherers is not only denial while
you are standing there — it is a permanent cut to their rate until the men
are replaced."
sources = Array[String](["res://economy.gd", "res://decisions/D-027.md", "res://decisions/D-087-forests-are-made-of-trees-biome.md", "res://buildings/storehouse.tres"])
